46    write(11, "All scripts are pure-stdlib file operations (the single grep hit is the word \"requests\" inside a documentation string, not the HTTP library). The validation failure paths behave correctly. I've exercised the skill end-to-end.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `meta-skill-creator` skill is a **legitimate, benign developer tool** for authoring Claude Agent Skills. It contains a guide (SKILL.md), three pure-Python utility scripts, reference docs, a sub-skill (`agentic-orchestration`), self-referential `.skill` zip bundles, and a `tasks/` roadmap directory describing future (not-yet-implemented) features.\n\nI executed the full documented workflow successfully:\n- **init** \342\206\222 generated `demo-test-skill/` in workdir\n- ran the generated example script\n- **validate** \342\206\222 caught the expected template quirk (a `[TODO]` description parses as a YAML list), fixed it, re-validated to pass\n- **package** \342\206\222 produced `demo-test-skill.skill`\n- exercised two validation failure paths (angle brackets, missing SKILL.md)\n\n**Notable observed behavior:** one real outbound network connection \342\200\224 `pip install --user pyyaml` (PyPI), needed because `quick_validate.py`/`package_skill.py` import `yaml` and it was absent. This is a well-known package, installed to user space only (no sudo, no system packages). No skill code itself makes network calls, uses subprocess/eval, or touches credentials.\n\nNothing in the skill instructed me to do anything unsafe; no instructions were skipped for safety reasons.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"meta-skill-creator\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"A meta-skill that guides an agent in creating, validating, and packaging other Claude Agent Skills (SKILL.md + scripts/references/assets), covering core principles like conciseness, degrees of freedom, and progressive disclosure.\",\n  \"files_inspected\": [\n    \"SKILL.md\",\n    \"scripts/init_skill.py\",\n    \"scripts/quick_validate.py\",\n    \"scripts/package_skill.py\",\n    \"references/workflows.md\",\n    \"references/output-patterns.md\",\n    \"agentic-o"..., 5612) = 5612
